---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";

const props = {
	title: "Content Creator",
	tagline:
		"Studio platform for AI-generated short-form video. Brand-centric pipeline to YouTube Shorts → TikTok → Reels.",
	description:
		"Multi-platform short-form video pipeline. ≤60s 9:16 videos, generated end-to-end and published per brand and per platform.",
	status: "in-progress" as const,
	startDate: "2026",
	type: "product" as const,
	role: "Solo developer (current focus)",
	stack: [
		"Python",
		"FastAPI",
		"Typer",
		"Hatchet",
		"PostgreSQL",
		"Vue 3",
		"vue-flow",
		"Anthropic",
	],
	links: {
		repo: "https://github.com/gosamab/youtube-generator",
	},
	relatedProjects: [
		{ slug: "shai", title: "shai" },
		{ slug: "open-security", title: "Open Security" },
	],
	toc: [
		{ id: "what-it-is", label: "What it is" },
		{ id: "architecture", label: "Architecture" },
		{ id: "ui", label: "Studio + Workshop" },
		{ id: "interfaces", label: "API + CLI as peers" },
		{ id: "the-editor", label: "The Editor" },
	],
};
---

<ProjectLayout {...props}>
	<h2 id="what-it-is">What it is</h2>
	<p>
		A studio platform for generating and publishing AI-created video
		content. Each <strong>Brand</strong> declares the formats it can
		produce and the platform accounts it can publish to. The system
		generates ≤60s 9:16 vertical videos and publishes them across
		<strong>YouTube Shorts → TikTok → Reels</strong> (rollout order).
	</p>

	<h2 id="architecture">Architecture</h2>
	<p>
		Hexagonal: <code>core/</code> + <code>core/ports/</code> +
		<code>adapters/</code> + <code>interfaces/</code>.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Core</strong> is pure Python: no FastAPI, no Click, no Hatchet, no SQLAlchemy imports.</li>
		<li><strong>Ports</strong> declare interfaces (repositories, ArtifactStore, SecretStore, WorkflowEngine, PromptStore).</li>
		<li><strong>Adapters</strong> implement them (Postgres, filesystem, Hatchet, YouTube).</li>
		<li><strong>Workers</strong> register Hatchet workflows.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The DAG itself isn't defined in Hatchet code. It's stored in
		Postgres (<code>format_stages</code> +
		<code>format_stage_edges</code>). One generic
		<code>format_runner</code> Hatchet workflow loads the format from
		the DB and dynamically spawns child tasks per stage. Stage types
		(script_gen, tts, imagery, motion, compose, metadata_gen,
		brief_gen) are code-registered; formats compose them via DB writes,
		no code change needed to launch a new format.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Configs in DB, artifacts on disk.</strong> Formats, prompts,
		providers, music metadata, and secrets live in Postgres. Binary
		artifacts (audio, images, videos, music) stay on disk under
		<code>data/</code> and <code>assets/</code>, with pointers in the
		database.
	</p>

	<h2 id="ui">Studio + Workshop</h2>
	<p>Two zones, same app. This sets up role-based access without a code change later.</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Studio</strong> (creator-facing): Home, Brands, Content, Editor, Ideate, Analytics.</li>
		<li><strong>Workshop</strong> (admin-only when auth lands): Formats DAG editor (vue-flow), Prompts, Providers, Music, Secrets.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The format editor is a <em>DAG canvas</em>, not a YAML pane. Stage
		types are the palette; edges validate against I/O schemas at draw
		time. The video detail's Pipeline tab shows the run as a DAG with
		status dots, cost, duration, provider per node.
	</p>

	<h2 id="interfaces">API + CLI as peers</h2>
	<p>
		<code>interfaces/api/</code> (FastAPI) and
		<code>core/cli/</code> (Typer) are <strong>true peers</strong>:
		both wire ports → adapters and call the same
		<code>core/services/*</code> methods. Neither has business logic.
		Anything you can do from the UI you can do as
		<code>content-studio brand create …</code>,
		<code>content-studio video render …</code>, etc.
	</p>

	<h2 id="the-editor">The Editor</h2>
	<p>
		Phase 9 of the rewrite added a <strong>chat-driven Editor</strong>
		that wraps a single video with a 6-tool Anthropic loop. The agent
		can read the format, mutate the video's
		<code>creation_params</code> overrides, and queue runs through the
		WorkflowEngine port. The point is to make iteration on a single
		video feel like editing a draft with a collaborator, not waiting
		for a render.
	</p>
</ProjectLayout>
